        [
          "AQUALOCK FLEXI TECHNICAL DATA SHEET VER NO. N.1",
          "",
          "",
          "",
          "",
          ""
        ],
        [
          "APPLICATION: \u0178 Slurry can be applied by brush or trowel with the recommended coverage at the approximate rate of 1.8-2kg/m2/ 2 coats, to achieve 1.2-1.5 mm DFT (minimum two coat should be applied). \u0178 Allow the slurry to cure for at least 4 -6 hours before applying a second coat \u0178 After the application of second coat for providing mechanical key for the protective screed/ plaster, some coursed sand conforming to zone 2/zone 3 should be sprinkled. Allow it to cure for min. 12 to 24 hrs. \u0178 Once the second coat is cured, clean the second coat by with the help of soft broom/brush to remove excess sand before moist curing. \u0178 For efflorescence\u2014 apply 2-3 coats of Trubuild Aqualock Flexi on clean bricks followed by plaster using Trubuild IW 111. MIXING: \u0178 Slowly add powder Part B to liquid Part A in a clean container and mix until a smooth and homogenous slurry mixture is achieved. \u0178 Allow the mixed slurry to stand for 5-6 minutes for releasing entrapped air during the mixing, prior to application. Mixed material must be used within recommended pot life. CURING: \u0178 For maximum protection, allow min. 12 to 24 hours curing time after the second coat. After application of the 2nd coat, allow the system to air cure for min. 5 to 6 hours. This should be followed by moist curing by sprinkling /spraying of potable \u0178 water for 24 hours. After moist curing, the surface should be allowed to air cure for min. 3 to 5 days before covering it with screed. \u0178 Trubuild Aqualock Flexi requires at least 7 days curing before any ponding test. For any water retaining structure, the final water should be filled after 7 days. PRECAUTIONS \u0178 Trubuild Aqualock Flexi is not for decorative treatment. \u0178 Avoid application in afternoon and during strong winds. Do not add water in the mix under any circumstances. Apply only to sound, prepared substrates and surfaces which should be well dampened but free of surface water and leaks. Do not exceed maximum layer thickness. \u0178 For waterproofing or damp proofing application, always use at least 2 coats to give a total thickness of between 1.2-1.5 mm. In areas of severe water penetration, three coats might be required. \u0178 Additional coats may be required from negative side. \u0178 Protect freshly applied material from freezing conditions, rains, winds, direct sunlight, etc. \u0178 Avoid open to sky application during intermittent rain or on a substrate subjected to standing/ run off water. \u0178 Trubuild Aqualock Flexi does not provide a trafficable finish. In case the roof needs to be made trafficable, a screed needs to be laid on the finished system followed by a suitable bonding layer. \u0178 New concrete substrate should be fully cured min. 28 days before application of Trubuild Aqualock Flexi. TECHNICAL PROPERTIES S.NO. PROPERTIES STANDARD RESULTS Mixing ratio - 1:1.4 (Part A liquid:Part Bpowder) by weight 1. Set to touch time at 25-27\u00b0C (min.) ASTM D1640:2018 45 2. Adhesion to concrete after 7 days (Mpa) ASTM D 4541:2017 \u22651 3. Tensile strength \u2013 on casting (N/mm2) ASTM D 412:2016 \u22651 4. Elongation at break (%) ASTM D 412:2016 >150 5. Crack bridging ability (mm) EN 1062-7:2004 Up to 2 6. Rapid chloride penetration test (coulombs) ASTM C 1202: 2019 <2500 7. Food grade certification CFTRI certification Pass 8. Toxicity IS 6582:1972 Non -toxic 9. Water penetration at 5 bar pressure EN12390-8:2019 NIL 10. Shore A hardness ASTM D 2240:2015 70 11. Negative permeability ASTM D-7088:2017 up to 4 bar 12. Anti-efflorescence SS-500:2015 Pass",
